{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pulls/16","id":5021555083,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVOzNm88AAAABK07Ziw","html_url":"https://github.com/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pull/16","diff_url":"https://github.com/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pull/16.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pull/16.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/issues/16","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pulls/16/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pulls/16/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/issues/16/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/statuses/6622e434ad86fc8b7b7a2d4e2aafddec530cb62b","number":16,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Keep Books Compendium lore visible without voice packs","user":{"login":"z1xel","id":121463840,"node_id":"U_kgDOBz1kIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121463840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel","html_url":"https://github.com/z1xel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem\nRemoving the optional Books sound-pack addon can make the Books Compendium look empty when a prior `Voiced Only` filter preference is enabled. Quests and Zones' bundled lore text continues to work without recordings; Books' text is also bundled in `SoftSpoken_Books/Data/Books.lua`.\n\n## Fix\n- Make Books' **Voiced Only** filter ineffective when there are no compatible packs with any recordings, without changing the stored user preference.\n- Grey out the filter entry when unavailable, re-enabling it automatically when a pack returns.\n- Invalidate cached pack availability when refreshing the list, without re-rendering the catalogue for every audio playback event.\n- Extend the shared Compendium filter menu with an **optional** disabled callback. Other modules' filters are unchanged.\n- Keep `Discovered Only`, `Unlock Unfound`, existing discovery/save data, and ordinary narration behavior as before.\n\n## In-game test on WoW 1.12\n- [ ] Set Books **Voiced Only** while a voice pack is installed, then disable/remove that pack and `/reload`. Books should still list writings; the Voiced Only option should be greyed out.\n- [ ] Select a *discovered* writing. Its bundled text should appear on the parchment and the play control should be unavailable.\n- [ ] With **Discovered Only** on, only discovered writings should show; with **Unlock Unfound** off, undiscovered writings should remain locked.\n- [ ] Reinstall the pack and reload: Voiced Only becomes available and the prior saved choice applies again.\n- [ ] Verify Quest and Places browsing, search, filter menu and playback remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Confirm no Lua errors and no excessive list redraws during playback.\n\n**Note:** this targets the identifiable audio-dependent *filtering* path. If Books is still empty with Voiced Only already off, troubleshoot corpus loading / discovery separately rather than weakening discovery restrictions.\n\n**Status:** source review completed; in-game test outstanding.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-26T17:09:40Z","updated_at":"2026-10-26T17:43:55Z","closed_at":"2026-10-26T17:18:29Z",